(a) the specific initiatives implemented to establish comprehensive wayside amenities along National Highways, encompassing rest areas, refreshment zones and rapid-response emergency facilities;
(b) the progress achieved in the electric vehicle charging infrastructure along high-traffic National Highway corridors during the last three years;
(c) whether the strategic adoption of Public-Private Partnership models for these facilities has successfully stimulated rural entrepreneurship and local economic growth;
(d) if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the methodology through which trauma-care services and modern public-convenience infrastructure are being synchronised with the larger wayside amenities network?

(a) whether Government has observed that in several incentive and subsidy schemes, substantial public financial support has been extended without clearly defined requirements relating to domestic value addition, local sourcing and indigenous manufacturing;
(b) whether the Ministry has recently advised all Ministries and Departments to incorporate such requirements at the scheme-design stage itself rather than during implementation; and
(c) if so, the details of salient features of the proposed framework, and the manner in which compliance with these requirements would be monitored and evaluated?

(a) whether it is a fact that the total quantity of Wheat and Rice held in the Central Pool as on 1st April, 2026 exceeded the prescribed buffer norms;
(b) whether the quantum of wheat procurement achieved during the Rabi Marketing Season 2026–27 is higher as compared to the previous season;
(c) whether Government has data on the number of farmers who benefited through Minimum Support Price (MSP) operations during the Rabi Marketing Season 2026–27;
(d) whether Government has taken steps to ensure efficient utilisation of surplus foodgrain stocks so as to optimise storage costs; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has approved the development of a strategic petroleum reserve (SPR) project by ONGC as part of its efforts to expand the country's emergency crude oil stockpile;
(b) whether ONGC has accorded in-principle approval for the development of a strategic petroleum reserve at Mangalore in accordance with the directions of the Ministry of Petroleum and Natural Gas, if so, the capacity of such Strategic Petroleum Reserve;
(c) whether Government has directed ONGC to explore commercial utilisation opportunities for the proposed strategic petroleum reserve project with associated regulatory support; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has implemented schemes to promote agricultural mechanisation and provide modern agricultural machinery to farmers across the country;
(b) if so, the details of the number and value of agricultural machines distributed, including under the Sub-Mission on Agricultural Mechanisation (SMAM), since 2021-22;
(c) whether Government has taken special measures to increase access to farm equipment in underserved regions and the North-Eastern States;
(d) whether financial assistance has been provided for promoting drone-based precision agriculture; and
(e) whether Government has assessed the impact of these initiatives on productivity, cost reduction, sustainable farming and farmers’ incomes?

(a) whether it is a fact that the 1st and 2nd BRICS Cultural Working Group (CWG) meetings deliberated on safeguarding the intellectual property rights of traditional artisans and cultural practitioners in the era of artificial intelligence;
(b) whether any decisions were taken to enhance cooperation among BRICS member States for the identification, recovery and return of stolen cultural artefacts and antiquities;
(c) whether Government has prepared an action plan for implementing the recommendations and cultural initiatives adopted during the BRICS Cultural Working Group meetings and the Varanasi Ministerial Meeting; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has taken note of reports highlighting the poor state of Industrial Training Institutes (ITIs) in Karnataka, where many trainees are reportedly completing courses without obtaining the prescribed credentials;
(b) whether nearly half of the trainer posts in Government ITIs in Karnataka are vacant and only a small proportion of registered enterprises are engaging apprentices, thereby affecting the quality of vocational training and employability of trainees; and
(c) whether Government proposes to upgrade more ITIs in Karnataka under the National Scheme for Industrial Training Institute (ITI) Upgradation and take to fill trainer vacancies, if so, the details thereof?

(a) the criteria and parameters adopted for the selection of Model Solar Villages under the PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijlee Yojana in the country, especially in Tripura, Jharkhand and Uttar Pradesh;
(b) the number of Model Solar Villages selected across the country and the progress achieved so far, State-wise including district-wise details of Tripura, Jharkhand and Uttar Pradesh;
(c) the financial assistance and other incentives provided by Government to promote the installation of rooftop solar systems in rural areas; and
(d) the manner in which the Model Solar Village initiative is contributing to rural energy access, clean energy adoption and sustainable development in the country including Tripura, Jharkhand and Uttar Pradesh?

(a) whether Central Government has undertaken measures to expand medical education capacity in Karnataka through the upgradation and strengthening of Government Medical Colleges;
(b) if so, the details of infrastructure projects sanctioned, including teaching hospitals, laboratories, hostels and academic blocks;
(c) the total Central share allocated and released for such projects during the last five years; 
(d) whether Government proposes similar support for other States to increase the availability of doctors and specialists in the country; and
(e) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has launched or approved an Artificial Intelligence based pilot through the National Payments Corporation of India (NPCI) to detect and prevent digital payment frauds before funds are siphoned off; 
(b) whether the AI-based fraud detection system is designed to identify suspicious transactions, mule accounts and fraudulent fund flows in real time and enable timely intervention by banks and NPCI; 
(c) whether Government proposes to scale up the AI-based fraud detection framework across banks and digital payment platforms after completion of the pilot; and
(d) if so, the details thereof?

(a) whether Government has conducted any assessment regarding employment, labour force participation, unemployment and earnings in India's million-plus cities vis-à-vis the rest of urban India, if so, the details and key findings thereof;
(b) whether workers in million-plus cities have higher participation in regular salaried employment and higher average earnings than workers in other urban areas;
(c) whether unemployment rates in million-plus cities differ from those in the rest of urban India; and
(d) if so, the steps being taken to promote quality employment and reduce unemployment across all urban centres?

(a) whether the expansion of the National PNG Drive 2.0 accelerated the targeted gasification of residential schools, colleges and hostels in North India;
(b) if so, the details thereof;
(c) the number of commercial kitchens that have switched from LPG to PNG since January;
(d) the total number of new domestic PNG connections provided during the special three-month accelerated approval framework period; and
(e) the specific criteria used by the Petroleum and Natural Gas Regulatory Board to monitor the pricing model for priority PNG connections?
